# Feature-flag delivery (Software Development center)

**On-demand rule.** Load when **`master-planner`**, **`pr-breakdown`**, **`delivery-phases`**, **`phase-planner`**, or mission plans reference feature-flag planning.

## Purpose (binding)

A feature flag hides **unfinished feature work** from end users until the feature is ready.

| Allowed | Forbidden |
|---------|-----------|
| Gate incomplete UX behind a boolean until graduation | App configuration, environment toggles, kill switches unrelated to feature readiness |
| Temporary developer opt-in via Settings for dogfooding | Permanent product settings disguised as flags |

**Type:** Always **boolean** (`sedea.features.<flagId>`).

## When to ask (binding)

| Delivery shape | Action |
|----------------|--------|
| **PR count K = 1** | No new flag — auto `newFeatureFlag: false`; no AskQuestion |
| **PR count K > 1** or multi-phase **N > 1** | Ask via **`master-planner`** Step **7c.5** — recommend yes when hiding unfinished UX |

**Trigger unchanged:** more than one PR in total ⇒ ask whether a flag is required.

## When the developer chooses yes

Scaffold delivery in this order:

| Stage | Concern |
|-------|---------|
| **Intro (first PR or before feature code)** | Add registry entry + Settings key; **`developDefault: false`**, **`packagedBuildDefault: false`**. End users see current behavior; developers opt in via Settings for dogfooding. |
| **Feature work (middle)** | Existing breakdown PRs or phases; all flag-gated code reads the registry. |
| **Graduation (last PR or last phase)** | Remove registry entry + consumer guards; behavior **on by default** for all installs (hard-wire or lifecycle `removed`). |

**Multi-phase delivery:** append a final **Feature flag graduation** phase at the end of the approved phase list (same graduation concern as the last PR above).

**Early enable (explicit only):** on developer request, a named prior PR or phase may flip defaults to **ON** before graduation — document in plan Changes and PR Caveats; do not infer from prose alone.

## Implementation alignment

When the target repo includes **`.cursor/rules/feature-flags-contract.mdc`** (or equivalent), follow that registry / `sedea.features.*` / lifecycle wording for implementation bullets. **This center rule is planning policy** — it does not edit the runtime registry.

